1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,356
Today your scripts learn to fail well.

2
00:00:02,906 --> 00:00:05,796
Every script meets trouble: a missing file,

3
00:00:05,796 --> 00:00:06,602
a bad value,

4
00:00:06,602 --> 00:00:08,080
a server that is busy.

5
00:00:08,080 --> 00:00:12,314
Three habits turn a crash into a controlled result: exceptions,

6
00:00:12,314 --> 00:00:12,852
logging,

7
00:00:12,852 --> 00:00:13,658
and retries.

8
00:00:14,208 --> 00:00:17,493
Every demo is typed live on Ubuntu twenty-four oh four.

9
00:00:19,543 --> 00:00:21,105
When something goes wrong,

10
00:00:21,105 --> 00:00:22,728
Python raises an exception.

11
00:00:22,728 --> 00:00:24,049
If nothing catches it,

12
00:00:24,049 --> 00:00:26,092
the script stops with a traceback.

13
00:00:26,642 --> 00:00:28,318
Try holds the risky code.

14
00:00:28,318 --> 00:00:31,066
Except handles one named kind of failure.

15
00:00:31,066 --> 00:00:33,076
Else runs when nothing failed,

16
00:00:33,076 --> 00:00:34,685
and finally always runs.

17
00:00:35,235 --> 00:00:38,832
Logging is how a script tells operators what happened.

18
00:00:38,832 --> 00:00:40,231
It has levels: debug,

19
00:00:40,231 --> 00:00:40,564
info,

20
00:00:40,564 --> 00:00:41,097
warning,

21
00:00:41,097 --> 00:00:41,763
and error.

22
00:00:42,313 --> 00:00:47,497
Retries handle temporary failures. Wait, try again, and wait longer each time.

23
00:00:48,047 --> 00:00:52,975
The rule: catch what you expect, say what happened, and retry only what can recover.

24
00:00:55,025 --> 00:00:59,356
First, an exception. Start Python. Type: python three, dash Q.

25
00:01:00,206 --> 00:01:02,999
Ask Python to turn a word into a number.

26
00:01:02,999 --> 00:01:03,698
Type: int,

27
00:01:03,698 --> 00:01:04,605
open bracket,

28
00:01:04,605 --> 00:01:05,025
quote,

29
00:01:05,025 --> 00:01:05,444
eight,

30
00:01:05,444 --> 00:01:05,863
quote,

31
00:01:05,863 --> 00:01:06,840
close bracket.

32
00:01:07,390 --> 00:01:08,205
A traceback.

33
00:01:08,205 --> 00:01:09,835
Read it from the bottom.

34
00:01:09,835 --> 00:01:12,144
The last line names the exception,

35
00:01:12,144 --> 00:01:12,959
value error,

36
00:01:12,959 --> 00:01:13,842
and says why.

37
00:01:13,842 --> 00:01:16,491
The lines above show where it happened.

38
00:01:16,491 --> 00:01:17,374
Leave Python.

39
00:01:17,374 --> 00:01:18,121
Type: exit,

40
00:01:18,121 --> 00:01:18,460
open,

41
00:01:18,460 --> 00:01:18,868
close.

42
00:01:19,418 --> 00:01:24,047
Now a script that expects trouble. Show it. Type: cat load dot P Y.

43
00:01:24,597 --> 00:01:27,393
It tries to open settings dot jay son.

44
00:01:27,393 --> 00:01:30,630
Each except block handles one named failure.

45
00:01:30,630 --> 00:01:32,764
Else runs when all went well,

46
00:01:32,764 --> 00:01:34,530
and finally always runs.

47
00:01:34,530 --> 00:01:35,045
Run it,

48
00:01:35,045 --> 00:01:36,664
with no settings file.

49
00:01:36,664 --> 00:01:38,062
Type: python three,

50
00:01:38,062 --> 00:01:39,018
load dot P Y.

51
00:01:39,568 --> 00:01:40,614
File not found,

52
00:01:40,614 --> 00:01:41,172
handled.

53
00:01:41,172 --> 00:01:44,032
The script chose defaults and carried on.

54
00:01:44,032 --> 00:01:46,333
Now create a valid settings file.

55
00:01:46,333 --> 00:01:47,100
Type: echo,

56
00:01:47,100 --> 00:01:49,541
then the jay son with retries five,

57
00:01:49,541 --> 00:01:50,727
in single quotes,

58
00:01:50,727 --> 00:01:53,307
redirected into settings dot jay son.

59
00:01:53,857 --> 00:01:59,958
No output, the file is written. Run the script again. Type: python three, load dot P Y.

60
00:02:00,508 --> 00:02:01,704
Loaded settings,

61
00:02:01,704 --> 00:02:02,601
finally ran,

62
00:02:02,601 --> 00:02:04,095
and retries is five.

63
00:02:04,095 --> 00:02:06,337
Now break the file on purpose.

64
00:02:06,337 --> 00:02:07,159
Type: echo,

65
00:02:07,159 --> 00:02:08,131
single quote,

66
00:02:08,131 --> 00:02:08,953
open brace,

67
00:02:08,953 --> 00:02:09,252
bad,

68
00:02:09,252 --> 00:02:10,223
single quote,

69
00:02:10,223 --> 00:02:12,988
redirected into settings dot jay son.

70
00:02:13,538 --> 00:02:17,485
Run it one more time. Type: python three, load dot P Y.

71
00:02:18,035 --> 00:02:18,848
Bad jay son,

72
00:02:18,848 --> 00:02:20,272
caught and explained,

73
00:02:20,272 --> 00:02:21,220
with no crash.

74
00:02:21,220 --> 00:02:23,999
Catch the specific exceptions you expect.

75
00:02:23,999 --> 00:02:26,032
A bare except hides real bugs,

76
00:02:26,032 --> 00:02:26,846
so avoid it.

77
00:02:28,896 --> 00:02:29,776
Now logging.

78
00:02:29,776 --> 00:02:31,170
Print is for users.

79
00:02:31,170 --> 00:02:33,003
Logging is for operators,

80
00:02:33,003 --> 00:02:34,617
because it has levels.

81
00:02:34,617 --> 00:02:35,790
Show the script.

82
00:02:35,790 --> 00:02:37,771
Type: cat log demo dot P Y.

83
00:02:38,321 --> 00:02:40,109
The level is set to info,

84
00:02:40,109 --> 00:02:42,611
so the debug line will stay hidden.

85
00:02:42,611 --> 00:02:46,616
Log dot exception records the message and the traceback.

86
00:02:46,616 --> 00:02:47,117
Run it.

87
00:02:47,117 --> 00:02:48,476
Type: python three,

88
00:02:48,476 --> 00:02:49,691
log demo dot P Y.

89
00:02:50,541 --> 00:02:50,916
Info,

90
00:02:50,916 --> 00:02:51,516
warning,

91
00:02:51,516 --> 00:02:51,967
error,

92
00:02:51,967 --> 00:02:53,992
each tagged with its level.

93
00:02:53,992 --> 00:02:55,867
The debug line is hidden,

94
00:02:55,867 --> 00:02:58,718
and the error came with its traceback,

95
00:02:58,718 --> 00:03:00,668
so you can find the cause.

96
00:03:00,668 --> 00:03:02,543
Now turn the detail down.

97
00:03:02,543 --> 00:03:03,293
Type: sed,

98
00:03:03,293 --> 00:03:03,818
dash I,

99
00:03:03,818 --> 00:03:04,268
quote,

100
00:03:04,268 --> 00:03:04,868
S slash,

101
00:03:04,868 --> 00:03:05,468
I N F O,

102
00:03:05,468 --> 00:03:05,919
slash,

103
00:03:05,919 --> 00:03:06,969
W A R N I N G,

104
00:03:06,969 --> 00:03:07,419
slash,

105
00:03:07,419 --> 00:03:07,869
quote,

106
00:03:07,869 --> 00:03:09,144
log demo dot P Y.

107
00:03:09,694 --> 00:03:14,686
No output. Run it again. Type: python three, log demo dot P Y.

108
00:03:15,236 --> 00:03:17,902
Now only the warning and the error appear.

109
00:03:17,902 --> 00:03:18,536
Same code,

110
00:03:18,536 --> 00:03:19,235
less noise.

111
00:03:19,235 --> 00:03:22,599
In production you lower the level to keep logs short,

112
00:03:22,599 --> 00:03:25,455
and raise the detail when you hunt a problem.

113
00:03:27,505 --> 00:03:27,880
Last,

114
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:28,480
retries.

115
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:32,303
A busy server or a dropped connection is temporary.

116
00:03:32,303 --> 00:03:34,927
This script tries up to four times,

117
00:03:34,927 --> 00:03:36,351
logs every attempt,

118
00:03:36,351 --> 00:03:38,375
and waits longer each time.

119
00:03:38,375 --> 00:03:38,975
Show it.

120
00:03:38,975 --> 00:03:40,774
Type: cat retry dot P Y.

121
00:03:41,324 --> 00:03:43,426
The wait doubles: one second,

122
00:03:43,426 --> 00:03:43,716
two,

123
00:03:43,716 --> 00:03:44,078
four.

124
00:03:44,078 --> 00:03:45,818
That is called back off.

125
00:03:45,818 --> 00:03:46,978
Our lab address,

126
00:03:46,978 --> 00:03:47,412
flaky,

127
00:03:47,412 --> 00:03:49,369
fails twice and then works.

128
00:03:49,369 --> 00:03:49,877
Run it.

129
00:03:49,877 --> 00:03:51,254
Type: python three,

130
00:03:51,254 --> 00:03:52,268
retry dot P Y.

131
00:03:56,318 --> 00:03:57,247
Two warnings,

132
00:03:57,247 --> 00:03:59,391
then success on attempt three.

133
00:03:59,391 --> 00:04:01,248
Now let it give up sooner,

134
00:04:01,248 --> 00:04:02,892
with only two attempts.

135
00:04:02,892 --> 00:04:03,606
Type: sed,

136
00:04:03,606 --> 00:04:04,106
dash I,

137
00:04:04,106 --> 00:04:04,535
quote,

138
00:04:04,535 --> 00:04:05,107
S slash,

139
00:04:05,107 --> 00:04:05,535
range,

140
00:04:05,535 --> 00:04:06,464
open bracket,

141
00:04:06,464 --> 00:04:06,750
one,

142
00:04:06,750 --> 00:04:07,179
comma,

143
00:04:07,179 --> 00:04:07,536
five,

144
00:04:07,536 --> 00:04:08,536
close bracket,

145
00:04:08,536 --> 00:04:08,965
slash,

146
00:04:08,965 --> 00:04:09,394
range,

147
00:04:09,394 --> 00:04:10,322
open bracket,

148
00:04:10,322 --> 00:04:10,608
one,

149
00:04:10,608 --> 00:04:11,037
comma,

150
00:04:11,037 --> 00:04:11,466
three,

151
00:04:11,466 --> 00:04:12,466
close bracket,

152
00:04:12,466 --> 00:04:12,895
slash,

153
00:04:12,895 --> 00:04:13,323
quote,

154
00:04:13,323 --> 00:04:14,324
retry dot P Y.

155
00:04:14,874 --> 00:04:19,716
No output. Run it again. Type: python three, retry dot P Y.

156
00:04:23,766 --> 00:04:25,153
Both attempts failed,

157
00:04:25,153 --> 00:04:28,057
and the script gave up with a clear message,

158
00:04:28,057 --> 00:04:28,849
not a crash.

159
00:04:28,849 --> 00:04:30,433
Now check its exit code.

160
00:04:30,433 --> 00:04:31,159
Type: echo,

161
00:04:31,159 --> 00:04:31,952
dollar sign,

162
00:04:31,952 --> 00:04:32,876
question mark.

163
00:04:33,426 --> 00:04:33,706
One.

164
00:04:33,706 --> 00:04:35,318
Not zero means failure,

165
00:04:35,318 --> 00:04:36,930
so any caller can tell.

166
00:04:36,930 --> 00:04:39,033
Retry only temporary problems,

167
00:04:39,033 --> 00:04:41,697
like timeouts and five hundred errors.

168
00:04:41,697 --> 00:04:45,272
A wrong token or a missing page never fixes itself,

169
00:04:45,272 --> 00:04:46,183
so fail fast.

170
00:04:48,233 --> 00:04:49,318
Here is your task,

171
00:04:49,318 --> 00:04:50,826
with everything you need.

172
00:04:50,826 --> 00:04:52,755
The files are in the repository,

173
00:04:52,755 --> 00:04:54,142
and in the description.

174
00:04:54,692 --> 00:05:00,367
The repository is git hub dot com, slash it dash waves, slash dev ops dash A I.

175
00:05:00,917 --> 00:05:05,788
In the academy slash lesson fifty-one folder you will find the task file,

176
00:05:05,788 --> 00:05:06,589
the lab API,

177
00:05:06,589 --> 00:05:07,657
and the checker,

178
00:05:07,657 --> 00:05:09,258
check fifty-one dot S H.

179
00:05:09,808 --> 00:05:11,100
You write one file,

180
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:12,459
fetch retry dot P Y.

181
00:05:12,459 --> 00:05:15,313
It calls the flaky address with a timeout,

182
00:05:15,313 --> 00:05:16,876
tries up to four times,

183
00:05:16,876 --> 00:05:17,828
and waits one,

184
00:05:17,828 --> 00:05:18,100
two,

185
00:05:18,100 --> 00:05:19,323
then four seconds.

186
00:05:19,873 --> 00:05:22,958
Every attempt is logged with the logging module.

187
00:05:22,958 --> 00:05:24,950
On success it prints recovered.

188
00:05:24,950 --> 00:05:28,807
After four failures it logs gave up and exits with code one,

189
00:05:28,807 --> 00:05:29,964
with no traceback.

190
00:05:30,514 --> 00:05:33,863
Do not open the solution file until you have really tried.

191
00:05:34,413 --> 00:05:38,104
The checker shows four pass lines. Write your results in a report.

192
00:05:40,154 --> 00:05:44,079
Here is how your work is judged. Six points, and you need all six.

193
00:05:44,629 --> 00:05:46,464
The checker shows four pass lines.

194
00:05:47,014 --> 00:05:49,211
Every attempt is logged at the right level.

195
00:05:49,761 --> 00:05:52,577
You catch request exception, never a bare except.

196
00:05:53,127 --> 00:05:56,562
Every call has a timeout, and the wait grows between attempts.

197
00:05:57,112 --> 00:06:01,507
After the last failure: a clear message, exit code one, no traceback.

198
00:06:02,057 --> 00:06:05,470
The report is complete, and you worked in your own virtual machine.

199
00:06:06,020 --> 00:06:07,641
To pass, you need all six.

200
